      U-Boot of Ambarella

This document describes how to compile the U-Boot and how to flash U-Boot
about the Ambarella CV5.

Table of Contents
+++++++++++++++++

  I - Introduction
  II - Nand Boot Build Options
  III - eMMC Boot Build Options
  IV - NOTE



I - Introduction
------------------

1) U-Boot
U-Boot is an open source Universal Boot Loader.
Please refer to https://www.denx.de/wiki/U-Boot for details.

2) Platform
Ambarella U-Boot code is used on CV5 platfrom, such as the CV5_timn EVK.


II - Nand Boot Build Options
------------------

1) build configuration
	a) config and build steps
        Demo:
	# cd ambarella/boards/cv5_timn
	# source ../../build/env/cortex-a76-linux5.15-gcc.env
        # make sync_build_mkcfg
        # make cv5_ipcam_uboot_config
	# make defconfig_public_linux
	# make -j8
	# make ambust
        # make ubootbst

	Firmware files:
	# ls ../../out/cv5_timn/images/
	cv5_timn_ambust_lpddr5_signed.bin
	u-boot.bin
	uboot_bst_release.bin

	# ls ../../out/cv5_timn/kernel/
	Image

	# ls ../../out/cv5_timn/rootfs/
	ubifs

	Binaries detail:
	cv5_timn_ambust_lpddr5_signed.bin:	use for dram initialization when in force usb mode.
	u-boot.bin:							u-boot binary
	uboot_bst_release.bin:				u-boot bst binary
	Image:								kernel binary
	ubifs:								file system binary

	b) Key menu for config
	There are several options in menuconfig can be selected when building U-Boot.
      	    	[*] Ambarella Boot Configuration  --->
			Bootloader (U-Boot) --->
					U-Boot Configuration  --->
		       U-Boot BST Options  --->
					USBstrap Configuration  --->

2) Firmware download
	a) use "fastboot" to download U-Boot related binaries to FLASH.
	Please refer to https://github.com/ARM-software/u-boot/blob/master/doc/README.android-fastboot for details.

	b) Tools (the site is for internal only)
	 http://yocto.ambarella.com/cv5_recovery/
	 Please refer to the Readme in the recovery directory.

	c) First time download binary for new blank flash
	  1) Enter force usb mode
          2) use the tool in item b)
          3) init the dram, command in pc client:
		pack_image_usb.exe -f cv5_timn_ambust_lpddr5_signed.bin

	  4) load u-boot binary to dram run in the board, like magic wand in Ambausb tool, command in pc client:
		fastboot.exe boot u-boot.bin --base 0x0

	  5) run related fastboot commands in the board
		# mtdparts
		device nand0 <amba_nand>, # parts = 4
 		#: name                size            offset          mask_flags
		0: bootstrap           0x00020000      0x00000000      0
		1: uboot               0x00100000      0x00020000      0
		2: kernel              0x01000000      0x00120000      0
		3: rootfs              0x08000000      0x01120000      0
	The parts names are one to one with the bianries.
		See items 6) command with 'fastboot.ext flash xxx(parts_name) xxx(binary_name)'

		# nand erase.chip
                # fastboot usb 0
             enter fastboot mode

	  6) run fastboot in the pc client, one by one.
		fastboot.exe flash bootstrap uboot_bst_release.bin
		fastboot.exe flash uboot u-boot.bin
		fastboot.exe flash kernel Image
		fastboot.exe flash rootfs ubifs
	  7) set board to normal boot from usb boot
		Power on

III - eMMC Boot Build Options
------------------

1) build configuration
	a) config and build steps
	change ini based on partition configuraion:
		such as uboot partiton start at 1M, then we should add below in ini
		<PARAM_BLD_MEDIA_START value="0x100000"/>
        Demo:
	# cd ambarella/boards/cv5_timn
	# source ../../build/env/cortex-a76-linux5.15-gcc.env
	# make sync_build_mkcfg
	# make cv5_ipcam_uboot_emmc_config
	# make defconfig_public_linux
	# make menuconfig_public_linux  (select CONFIG_EFI_PARTITION)
		-*- Enable the block layer  --->
			Partition Types  --->
				[*]   EFI GUID Partition support
	# make -j8
	# make ambust
	# make ubootbst

	Firmware files:
	# ls ../../out/cv5_timn/images/
	cv5_timn_ambust_lpddr5_signed.bin
	u-boot.bin
	uboot_bst_release.bin

	# ls ../../out/cv5_timn/kernel/
	Image

	# ls ../../out/cv5_timn/rootfs/
	ext4

	Binaries detail:
	cv5_timn_ambust_lpddr5_signed.bin:	use for dram initialization when in force usb mode.
	u-boot.bin:				u-boot binary
	uboot_bst_release.bin:			u-boot bst binary
	Image:					kernel binary
	ext4:					file system binary

	b) Key menu for config
	There are several options in menuconfig can be selected when building U-Boot.
		[*] Ambarella Boot Configuration  --->
			Bootloader (U-Boot) --->
				U-Boot Configuration  --->
			U-Boot BST Options  --->
					USBstrap Configuration  --->

2) Firmware download
	a) First time download binary for new blank flash
	  1) Enter force usb mode
	  2) use the tool in item b)
	  3) init the dram, command in pc client:
		pack_image_usb.exe -f cv5_timn_ambust_lpddr5_signed.bin

	  4) load u-boot binary to dram run in the board, like magic wand in Ambausb tool, command in pc client:
		fastboot.exe boot u-boot.bin --base 0x0

	  5) run related fastboot commands in the board
		See items 6) command with 'fastboot flash xxx(parts_name) xxx(binary_name)'

             # fastboot usb 0
             enter fastboot mode

	  6) run fastboot in the pc client, one by one.
		setup partition table
			fastboot oem cmd: gpt write mmc 0 ${partitions}
		setup bus width
			for 8bit bus width:
				fastboot oem cmd: mmc bootbus 0 2 1 0
			for 4bit bus width:
				fastboot oem cmd: mmc bootbus 0 1 1 0
		setup boot partition
			for boot partition1:
				fastboot oem cmd: mmc partconf 0 0 1 0
		setup RESET_n_FUNCTION
			fastboot oem cmd: mmc rst-function 0 1
		fastboot flash bst uboot_bst_release.bin
		fastboot flash uboot u-boot.bin
		fastboot flash kernel Image
		fastboot flash rootfs ext4
		ps: for rootfs, some times it is large, we need to change raw ext4 to android sparse image format, then flash
			img2simg ext4 ext4_s
			fastboot flash rootfs ext4_s
	  7) set board to normal boot from usb boot
		Power on

ps: if you want to u-boot at the same partition with bst, we can do like below
	change ini:
		<PARAM_BLD_MEDIA_START value="0x2000"/>
		<AMBOOT_EMMC_NEXT_FW_AREA value="BootPartition1"/>
	generate the new bst image which with u-boot.bin
		cat uboot_bst_release.bin u-boot.bin > bst_with_uboot.bin
	then flash bst_with_uboot.bin
		fastboot flash bst bst_with_uboot.bin

IV - Note
------------------
More U-Boot commands, please refer to the U-Boot or Linux community.

